      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, I understand the concerns. Here’s a version that should balance thoroughness with readability:\n\n---\n\n**Spinach Creamy Garlic Sauce Recipe (Thorough Edition)**\n\n1. In a medium-sized pan, **melt 1 tablespoon of butter** over medium heat. \n2. Once the **butter** is melted, add a **cup of chopped onions**, and cook until they become **soft and translucent**, which should take around 5 to 7 minutes.\n3. Next, **add 2 tablespoons of minced garlic** to the pan, stirring frequently to incorporate evenly with the softened onions.\n4. Pour in **3/4 cup of heavy cream**, along with a **pinch of salt** and a **dash of black pepper** to taste.\n5. Bring the mixture to a gentle simmer, allowing the flavors to meld together for about 10 minutes. If the sauce seems too thick, you can add a tablespoon of water to reach your desired consistency.\n6. Stir the **fresh spinach** into the sauce until it turns bright green and almost wilted, which usually takes about 2 to 3 minutes.\n7. This flavorful, creamy spinach garlic sauce is perfect drizzled over **cooked pasta**,",
